# 🔥 Smart LPG Cylinder Monitoring and Auto Booking System

An IoT-based solution to monitor LPG cylinder levels in real-time using a load cell, with automatic SMS and call alerts when the gas level is low. It includes buzzer-based local alerting and reset functionality after a refill is detected.

---

## 🧰 Components Used

| Component         | Description                                 |
|------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Arduino UNO R3    | Microcontroller for processing and control  |
| HX711 Module      | 24-bit ADC for load cell data               |
| Load Cell (10kg)  | Measures weight of the LPG cylinder         |
| SIM800L Module    | GSM module for SMS and call functionality   |
| Buzzer            | Audio alert for low gas level               |
| Push Button       | User acknowledgment/reset input             |
| LCD 1602 with I2C | Display weight and status messages          |
| Li-ion Battery    | Powers GSM module (3.7V, 2A recommended)    |
| Power Supply      | 5V/9V source (regulated for Arduino)        |

---

## 🔌 Hardware Connections

### 🏋️ Load Cell (10kg) to HX711 Module

| Load Cell Wire | HX711 Pin |
|----------------|-----------|
| Red            | E+        |
| Black          | E−        |
| Green          | A+        |
| White          | A−        |

---

### ⚙️ HX711 Module to Arduino Uno

| HX711 Pin | Arduino Uno Pin |
|-----------|------------------|
| VCC       | 5V               |
| GND       | GND              |
| DT        | D4               |
| SCK       | D5               |

---

### 🖥️ LCD 1602 with I2C to Arduino Uno

| I2C Pin | Arduino Uno Pin |
|---------|------------------|
| SDA     | A4               |
| SCL     | A5               |
| VCC     | 5V               |
| GND     | GND              |

---

### 📶 SIM800L GSM Module to Arduino & Battery

| SIM800L Pin | Connection                                   |
|-------------|----------------------------------------------|
| VCC         | Positive terminal of 3.7V Li-ion battery     |
| GND         | Ground terminal of 3.7V Li-ion battery       |
| TX          | RX pin of Arduino (e.g., D8 via SoftwareSerial) |
| RX          | TX pin of Arduino (e.g., D9 via SoftwareSerial) |

> ⚠️ **Note**: SIM800L is powered **only** by the 3.7V–4.2V battery, not from Arduino.  
> ⚠️ **Important**: Ensure your battery can provide at least **2A current** for stable operation.

---

### 🔋 Li-ion Rechargeable Battery (ICR18650 - 3.7V)

- Powers **only** the SIM800L GSM module.

